<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Maurepas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1699</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Old Biloxi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Maurepas was a French fort built in 1699 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-le-moyne-diberville">Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</a> on the eastern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biloxi">Biloxi</a> Bay, at present-day Ocean Springs, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>. It was the first seat of the French colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> and the base for exploring the lower Mississippi. The colony's headquarters moved to Mobile in 1702, and the fort was soon abandoned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-maurepas.jpg" alt="Fort Maurepas" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iberville · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_Maurepas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
